# Real offline study draft + durable approval. No discovery or model launch.
name: Paged finite study approval, cancel, resize and restart
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
type: run campaign:study {"campaignId":"offline-finite","scanInput":{"taskMode":"manual","tasks":["secret-scan"]}}
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 run receipt · completed | draft-completed
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 Study draft: offline-finite | draft-receipt
expect: 3 discovery jobs
expect: 1 worker
expect: No jobs started
ask: Does the draft disclose the fixed work and source identity while making review and approval the next step?
shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/study_approval.py @TMP_TARGET @ART/approval-command.txt
paste-file: @ART/approval-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 REVIEW PLAN & ALLOWANCE | work-terms
expect: Total provider calls: 9
expect: Protected review calls: 3
expect: 3 fixed jobs
expect: 1 attempt(s) each
expect: Plan digest: sha256:
expect: cancellation consume attempts
expect: starts no jobs
ask: Are the job count, attempt limits, full plan digest, model and allowance readable before approval?
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 REVIEW PLAN & ALLOWANCE | work-80
ask: At 80x24, are all approval terms reachable with visible paging and cancellation?
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 REVIEW PLAN & ALLOWANCE | work-60
keys: End
require-live-snap: 20 y approve | work-60-final
expect: starts no jobs
ask: At 60x20, does the last page keep the final terms and decision controls readable?
resize: 40x12
keys: Home
require-live-snap: 20 Read more to approve | work-40-first
keys: y
live-snap: hidden-work-cannot-approve
expect: REVIEW PLAN & ALLOWANCE
expect-not: y approve
expect: PgUp/PgDn read · Esc cancel
ask: Does the narrow first page make further reading and cancellation clear without enabling approval?
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 20 Dollar ceiling | work-40-middle
ask: Are the spending limits and uncertainty readable at 40x12?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 denied once | approval-canceled
ask: Does cancellation return to the prior surface without starting work?
paste-file: @ART/approval-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Read more to approve | reopened-first-page
expect: offline-finite
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 Total provider calls: 9 | work-tall
expect: Plan digest: sha256:
expect: y approve
ask: Is the complete approval readable at 96x89 without buried terms or misleading spending claims?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 Total provider calls: 9 | work-wide
expect: Protected review calls: 3
ask: Does the wide layout keep a comfortable reading width and clear decision controls?
resize: 40x12
keys: End
require-live-snap: 20 y approve | work-40-final
expect: starts no jobs
ask: Can the operator approve the finite plan from the final page at 40x12?
keys: y
resize: 120x36
require-live-snap: 25 Approved campaign: offline-finite | approved-work-receipt
expect: 3 fixed jobs
expect: 0/9
expect: no jobs started
ask: Does the durable receipt distinguish approved work from executed work and retain exact source provenance?
keys: C-c
env: NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: run campaign:allowance {"investigationId":"offline-finite"}
require-live-snap: 25 run receipt · completed | status-completed
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 25 Approved campaign: offline-finite | restored-work-receipt
expect: revision 1
expect: Unresolved calls: 0
expect: 0/9
ask: After restart without color, are the approved limits and unstarted work still inspectable?
shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/study_approval.py @TMP_TARGET @ART/approval-check.json --verify
keys: C-c
